# Environment variables for the adaptive agent harness.
#
# Nothing in `pnpm check` needs any of these. Every line is commented out, and
# the names are listed so they are discoverable ahead of the milestone that
# introduces them. Copy this file to `.env` and fill values in when you need
# them. Never commit `.env`.

# --- Milestone 1: AI Gateway credential ------------------------------------
# `pnpm example:run` is the ONE command in this repository that needs a model
# credential: `apps/example-agent` uses an AI Gateway model id, and the Gateway
# authenticates with Vercel OIDC or with an API key. Set either one. Without
# them the command exits 1 and points back at this file.
#
# `eve link` writes one of these into `.env.local` when the project is linked to
# a Vercel project, and `eve dev`'s `/login` stores one in the OS secret store
# instead. Neither is ever committed.
#
# `pnpm example:run:mock` needs NEITHER. It runs the same harness path against
# `apps/eve-fixture-agent`, whose model is eve's own `mockModel`, and the test
# helper that starts its server strips both names from the child environment so
# a logged-in machine cannot reach a provider by accident. `pnpm test:contract`
# does the same.
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=

# --- Milestone 1: the example agent ----------------------------------------
# The AI Gateway model id that apps/example-agent uses (agent/agent.ts). Leave
# it unset to take eve's own default for a scaffolded project,
# `openai/gpt-5.6-luna-fast`. This is a model id, not a credential.
# EXAMPLE_AGENT_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.6-luna-fast

# --- Milestone 1: choosing the example target ------------------------------
# `pnpm example:run:mock` passes `--mock` instead, so you never need this. It
# exists so a CI job or a shell can force the credential-free path without
# changing the command it runs.
# EXAMPLE_RUN_TARGET=mock

# --- Milestone 2: Supabase -------------------------------------------------
# `createSupabaseStorage()` reads the first and third of these (M2-T5), and
# `pnpm example:run` / `pnpm example:run:mock` check for both before deciding
# whether to record a durable run row and trace. Both or neither: a URL with no
# key cannot authenticate and a key with no URL has nowhere to go, so one of
# them alone counts as not configured, and the run says so on stderr and writes
# only its JSONL trace.
#
# Do NOT put local values here. `.env.example` is committed. Capture the local
# stack's values into the git-ignored `.env.local` with
# `pnpm exec supabase status -o env ...`; the example apps' `start` script
# loads that file with Node 24's `--env-file-if-exists`. The full command is in
# `docs/runbooks/supabase-local.md`.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# Optional. Only the row-level-security cases in the schema integration suite
# use it.
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-side only. It bypasses row-level security, so it must never reach a
# client, an agent tool or a trace.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
